(function() {
    'use strict';

    class AllianceLabAdapter extends USF.SimulationAdapter {
        constructor() {
            super();
            this.name = 'Alliance Lab: Trust, Control & Co-Development';
            this.version = '1.1.0';

            // Fixed board-approved innovation budget (EUR m) and the opportunity at stake.
            this.BUDGET = 12;                 // EUR 12,000,000
            this.OPPORTUNITY = 30;            // EUR 30,000,000 lost addressable revenue over 3 yrs if stalled

            // Bidault sweet spot: joint creativity peaks at a TRUST-LEANING configuration, not at
            // maximum trust and certainly not at maximum control. The dial is 0=full control, 100=full trust.
            this.CREATIVITY_PEAK_DIAL = 64;   // where the creativity curve tops out
            this.CREATIVITY_CURVE_WIDTH = 30; // gaussian width — how fast creativity falls off either side

            // Truth of the defection (hidden): it was an honest misunderstanding of an ambiguous IP term
            // the team itself may have left open — NOT an aggressive land-grab. (intent 0=accident .. 100=betrayal)
            this.DEFECTION_INTENT = 22;

            this.ROUNDS = [
                {
                    nameEn: 'Diagnose & Set Posture',
                    nameEs: 'Diagnosticar y Fijar la Postura',
                    briefingEn: `<strong>10 June 2026 — Munich. You have two weeks.</strong> Helbion Systems GmbH (EUR 380m revenue, 1,150 people, 12% R&D-to-sales) is strong in precision sensing hardware but <em>thin in the embedded AI</em> that is becoming the basis of competition. The board has approved a fixed <strong>EUR 12,000,000</strong> innovation budget and mandated Helbion's first serious co-development alliance — with <strong>Cortexa AI SAS</strong> (Toulouse, 140 people, leading-edge AI). A direct rival, <strong>Sentek</strong>, is rumored to be courting Cortexa too.<br><br>But Helbion is a <em>build-it-all-ourselves</em> culture, burned a decade ago when a joint project leaked a core design to a competitor. That scar makes the firm instinctively control-heavy — and that instinct is the trap. Research (Bidault, ESMT) is clear: excessive control signals distrust and <em>suppresses the very joint creativity the alliance exists to produce</em>. The goal is not minimum risk — it is the trust-control configuration that <strong>maximizes joint creativity given the risks</strong>.<br><br>Diagnose the alliance: how much does Helbion truly depend on Cortexa, and where is the real risk versus the real prize? Then set your opening position on the <strong>0–100 trust-control dial</strong> and justify it against both the upside and the firm's scar tissue.`,
                    briefingEs: `<strong>10 de junio de 2026 — Múnich. Tiene dos semanas.</strong> Helbion Systems GmbH (EUR 380m de ingresos, 1.150 personas, I+D/ventas del 12%) es fuerte en hardware de sensores de precisión pero <em>débil en la IA embebida</em> que se está convirtiendo en la base de la competencia. El consejo aprobó un presupuesto de innovación fijo de <strong>EUR 12.000.000</strong> y ordenó la primera alianza seria de co-desarrollo de Helbion — con <strong>Cortexa AI SAS</strong> (Toulouse, 140 personas, IA de vanguardia). Un rival directo, <strong>Sentek</strong>, también cortejaría a Cortexa.<br><br>Pero Helbion tiene una cultura de <em>hacerlo todo internamente</em>, escarmentada hace una década cuando un proyecto conjunto filtró un diseño clave a un competidor. Esa cicatriz vuelve a la empresa instintivamente control-céntrica — y ese instinto es la trampa. La investigación (Bidault, ESMT) es clara: el exceso de control señala desconfianza y <em>suprime la misma creatividad conjunta que la alianza existe para producir</em>. El objetivo no es el riesgo mínimo — es la configuración de confianza-control que <strong>maximiza la creatividad conjunta dado el riesgo</strong>.<br><br>Diagnostique la alianza: ¿cuánto depende Helbion realmente de Cortexa, y dónde está el riesgo real frente al premio real? Luego fije su posición inicial en el <strong>dial confianza-control de 0–100</strong> y justifíquela frente al potencial y a la cicatriz de la empresa.`,
                    eventEn: null,
                    eventEs: null
                },
                {
                    nameEn: 'Set the Mix & IP Terms',
                    nameEs: 'Fijar la Mezcla y los Términos de PI',
                    briefingEn: `Now design the governance architecture and price every choice against the <strong>EUR 12m</strong>. Each lever moves four gauges — <em>joint creativity, trust, IP risk, and the budget consumed by control machinery</em>.<br><br><strong>The IP-sharing tier</strong> runs from sharing only interfaces (crown jewels safe, but you starve Cortexa of what it needs to build — creativity stalls and mistrust breeds) to opening the core sensing models (creativity and trust soar — but with no architecture, your crown jewels can walk to Sentek). <strong>Control-machinery spend</strong> (audits, escrow, monitoring) buys a little IP-risk reduction but comes straight out of engineering: every euro on control is a euro not on innovation, and a gold-plated regime signals distrust that crowds out creativity. <strong>IP-term bounding</strong> — field-of-use limits, the background/foreground split, joint-ownership and patent sign-off rules — reduces risk cheaply and is the single most important architecture you can build.<br><br>Find the mix that <strong>maximizes innovation per euro</strong> without exposing Helbion to ruinous IP risk. And note carefully: an ambiguous IP term left open now is exactly the kind of gap that detonates later.`,
                    briefingEs: `Ahora diseñe la arquitectura de gobernanza y ponga precio a cada elección frente a los <strong>EUR 12m</strong>. Cada palanca mueve cuatro indicadores — <em>creatividad conjunta, confianza, riesgo de PI y el presupuesto consumido por la maquinaria de control</em>.<br><br><strong>El nivel de PI compartida</strong> va desde compartir solo interfaces (joyas de la corona a salvo, pero priva a Cortexa de lo que necesita para construir — la creatividad se estanca y crece la desconfianza) hasta abrir los modelos de sensado centrales (la creatividad y la confianza se disparan — pero sin arquitectura, sus joyas pueden irse a Sentek). El <strong>gasto en maquinaria de control</strong> (auditorías, escrow, monitoreo) compra algo de reducción de riesgo de PI pero sale directo de la ingeniería: cada euro en control es un euro no en innovación, y un régimen sobredimensionado señala desconfianza que ahoga la creatividad. El <strong>acotamiento de los términos de PI</strong> — límites de campo de uso, división background/foreground, reglas de copropiedad y de firma de patentes — reduce el riesgo de forma barata y es la arquitectura más importante que puede construir.<br><br>Encuentre la mezcla que <strong>maximice la innovación por euro</strong> sin exponer a Helbion a un riesgo de PI ruinoso. Y tenga cuidado: un término de PI ambiguo dejado abierto ahora es justo el tipo de hueco que detona después.`,
                    eventEn: `📡 <strong>Competitive signal:</strong> Cortexa's CEO mentions, almost in passing, that "another industrial player has reached out." Sentek is real. The clock on a beautifully-engineered-but-slow alliance is now running.`,
                    eventEs: `📡 <strong>Señal competitiva:</strong> El CEO de Cortexa menciona, casi de pasada, que "otro actor industrial nos ha contactado". Sentek es real. El reloj de una alianza bellamente diseñada pero lenta ya corre.`
                },
                {
                    nameEn: 'Respond to the Defection',
                    nameEs: 'Responder a la Defección',
                    briefingEn: `🚨 <strong>The shock.</strong> Cortexa has filed a patent on a <em>jointly-developed method</em> — without Helbion's sign-off. The facts are <strong>genuinely ambiguous</strong>: it could be an aggressive land-grab, or an honest misunderstanding of IP terms your own team may have left open in Round 2.<br><br>Your response sits on a spectrum from <strong>escalate / litigate / clamp down</strong> (demand the patent, re-impose control, threaten exit) to <strong>clarify / repair / recommit</strong> (treat it as a governance gap, renegotiate the rule, rebuild trust). Read the decision tree carefully: if you treat an ambiguous, possibly-accidental act as betrayal and clamp down, you may blow up a salvageable alliance over <em>a gap you left</em> — punishing the symptom, not the cause. But if you let it slide entirely to keep the peace, Cortexa learns it can act unilaterally with no consequence, and you signal that your IP terms are unenforceable.<br><br>Diagnose intent before you react. The right move addresses the <strong>root cause</strong> — and whether you can even do that depends on the IP bounding you set last round.`,
                    briefingEs: `🚨 <strong>El shock.</strong> Cortexa ha presentado una patente sobre un <em>método desarrollado conjuntamente</em> — sin la firma de Helbion. Los hechos son <strong>genuinamente ambiguos</strong>: podría ser una apropiación agresiva, o un malentendido honesto de unos términos de PI que su propio equipo pudo dejar abiertos en la Ronda 2.<br><br>Su respuesta se sitúa en un espectro desde <strong>escalar / litigar / endurecer</strong> (exigir la patente, re-imponer control, amenazar con salir) hasta <strong>aclarar / reparar / recomprometer</strong> (tratarlo como un hueco de gobernanza, renegociar la regla, reconstruir confianza). Lea el árbol de decisión con cuidado: si trata un acto ambiguo y posiblemente accidental como traición y endurece, puede volar una alianza salvable por <em>un hueco que usted dejó</em> — castigando el síntoma, no la causa. Pero si lo deja pasar del todo para mantener la paz, Cortexa aprende que puede actuar unilateralmente sin consecuencia, y usted señala que sus términos de PI son inaplicables.<br><br>Diagnostique la intención antes de reaccionar. La jugada correcta aborda la <strong>causa raíz</strong> — y si puede siquiera hacerlo depende del acotamiento de PI que fijó la ronda pasada.`,
                    eventEn: `📰 <strong>Ambiguity, not betrayal:</strong> A back-channel from Cortexa's engineers suggests they believed foreground IP was jointly filable — because the term sheet never said otherwise. Your own legal team admits the sign-off rule was left open. This was a gap, not a knife.`,
                    eventEs: `📰 <strong>Ambigüedad, no traición:</strong> Un canal informal de los ingenieros de Cortexa sugiere que creían que la PI foreground era patentable conjuntamente — porque el term sheet nunca dijo lo contrario. Su propio equipo legal admite que la regla de firma quedó abierta. Esto fue un hueco, no una puñalada.`
                },
                {
                    nameEn: 'Recover & Defend the ROI',
                    nameEs: 'Recuperar y Defender el ROI',
                    briefingEn: `🏛️ <strong>The board pitch.</strong> Helbion's board — scarred by the past leak and rattled by the patent incident — is tempted to revert to <em>build-it-all-ourselves</em>. You have one chance to recover the alliance and defend its ROI.<br><br>Set the recovered <strong>trust-control settlement</strong> after the defection, the joint-creativity targets, and the financial case: innovation value produced versus the EUR 12m spent, against the <strong>EUR 30m opportunity</strong> at stake. Your recovery governance choice runs from <em>kill the alliance and build internally</em> (forfeit the embedded-AI window) to a <strong>full relational-plus-contractual blend</strong> with staged real-options milestones and early-warning defection metrics — a durable capability, not a one-off survival.<br><br>The board will not approve a continuation unless trust has been re-established, joint creativity is real, IP risk is contained, and the ROI clears its bar. Make the crisis build something — and show them that <strong>trust is a strategy, not just a risk</strong>.`,
                    briefingEs: `🏛️ <strong>La presentación al consejo.</strong> El consejo de Helbion — marcado por la filtración pasada y sacudido por el incidente de la patente — está tentado de volver a <em>hacerlo todo internamente</em>. Tiene una oportunidad para recuperar la alianza y defender su ROI.<br><br>Fije el <strong>acuerdo confianza-control</strong> recuperado tras la defección, las metas de creatividad conjunta y el caso financiero: valor de innovación producido frente a los EUR 12m gastados, contra la <strong>oportunidad de EUR 30m</strong> en juego. Su elección de gobernanza de recuperación va desde <em>matar la alianza y construir internamente</em> (renunciar a la ventana de IA embebida) hasta una <strong>mezcla relacional-más-contractual completa</strong> con hitos escalonados de opciones reales y métricas de alerta temprana de defección — una capacidad duradera, no una supervivencia puntual.<br><br>El consejo no aprobará una continuación salvo que se haya restablecido la confianza, la creatividad conjunta sea real, el riesgo de PI esté contenido y el ROI supere su umbral. Haga que la crisis construya algo — y muéstreles que <strong>la confianza es una estrategia, no solo un riesgo</strong>.`,
                    eventEn: `🎙️ <strong>Skeptical board:</strong> "We were burned before. Why is more trust the answer and not more control?" Your settlement and your ROI case are the only credible reply — and only a real governance blend will hold the next time.`,
                    eventEs: `🎙️ <strong>Consejo escéptico:</strong> "Ya nos quemamos antes. ¿Por qué la respuesta es más confianza y no más control?" Su acuerdo y su caso de ROI son la única respuesta creíble — y solo una mezcla de gobernanza real aguantará la próxima vez.`
                }
            ];
        }

        initialize(state) {
            if (!state.domainState || Object.keys(state.domainState).length === 0) {
                state.domainState = {
                    creativity: 30,        // joint creativity output (0-100) — the prize
                    trust: 40,             // relational capital with Cortexa (0-100)
                    ipRisk: 25,            // exposure of crown jewels (0-100, lower better)
                    roi: 0,                // alliance ROI multiple (x)
                    controlSpend: 0,       // cumulative EUR m spent on control machinery
                    engBudget: 12,         // EUR m left for joint engineering
                    daysLeft: 14,          // competitive clock
                    sentekRisk: 0,         // cumulative risk Sentek signs Cortexa (0-100)
                    status: 'forming',     // 'forming' | 'thriving' | 'transactional' | 'lost' | 'dissolved'
                    rootCauseFixed: false, // did bounding/governance close the foreground sign-off gap
                    creativityHistory: [],
                    trustHistory: [],
                    ipRiskHistory: [],
                    roiHistory: []
                };
            }
            if (!state.decisions || Object.keys(state.decisions).length === 0) {
                state.decisions = {
                    trustControl: 50,
                    dependence: 50,
                    ipTier: 2,
                    controlSpend: 2,
                    ipBounding: 3,
                    defection: 3,
                    governance: 2
                };
            }
            this._updateBriefing(state);
        }

        validateDecisions(decisions) {
            var tcEl = document.getElementById('trustControlInput');
            var depEl = document.getElementById('dependenceInput');
            var tierEl = document.getElementById('ipTierInput');
            var spendEl = document.getElementById('controlSpendInput');
            var boundEl = document.getElementById('ipBoundingInput');
            var defEl = document.getElementById('defectionInput');
            var govEl = document.getElementById('governanceInput');

            if (tcEl) decisions.trustControl = parseInt(tcEl.value, 10);
            if (depEl) decisions.dependence = parseInt(depEl.value, 10);
            if (tierEl) decisions.ipTier = parseInt(tierEl.value, 10);
            if (spendEl) decisions.controlSpend = parseFloat(spendEl.value);
            if (boundEl) decisions.ipBounding = parseInt(boundEl.value, 10);
            if (defEl) decisions.defection = parseInt(defEl.value, 10);
            if (govEl) decisions.governance = parseInt(govEl.value, 10);

            if (!Number.isFinite(decisions.trustControl) || decisions.trustControl < 0 || decisions.trustControl > 100) {
                window.mySimulation.uiManager.showNotification(window.mySimulation.t('trustcontrol_warning'), 'warning');
                return false;
            }
            if (!Number.isFinite(decisions.dependence) || decisions.dependence < 0 || decisions.dependence > 100) {
                window.mySimulation.uiManager.showNotification(window.mySimulation.t('dependence_warning'), 'warning');
                return false;
            }
            if (!Number.isFinite(decisions.ipTier) || decisions.ipTier < 1 || decisions.ipTier > 4) {
                window.mySimulation.uiManager.showNotification(window.mySimulation.t('iptier_warning'), 'warning');
                return false;
            }
            if (!Number.isFinite(decisions.controlSpend) || decisions.controlSpend < 0 || decisions.controlSpend > 6) {
                window.mySimulation.uiManager.showNotification(window.mySimulation.t('controlspend_warning'), 'warning');
                return false;
            }
            if (!Number.isFinite(decisions.ipBounding) || decisions.ipBounding < 1 || decisions.ipBounding > 5) {
                window.mySimulation.uiManager.showNotification(window.mySimulation.t('ipbounding_warning'), 'warning');
                return false;
            }
            if (!Number.isFinite(decisions.defection) || decisions.defection < 1 || decisions.defection > 5) {
                window.mySimulation.uiManager.showNotification(window.mySimulation.t('defection_warning'), 'warning');
                return false;
            }
            if (!Number.isFinite(decisions.governance) || decisions.governance < 0 || decisions.governance > 5) {
                window.mySimulation.uiManager.showNotification(window.mySimulation.t('governance_warning'), 'warning');
                return false;
            }

            this._updateBriefing(window.mySimulation.state);
            return true;
        }

        calculateResults(state) {
            var d = state.decisions;
            var ds = state.domainState;
            var period = state.currentPeriod;

            // ----- Normalise levers -----
            var dial = d.trustControl;                 // 0 control .. 100 trust
            var trustLean = dial / 100;                // 0..1
            var tier = d.ipTier;                       // 1..4
            var tierNorm = (tier - 1) / 3;             // 0..1 (how much IP exposed)
            var spend = d.controlSpend;                // 0..6 EUR m on control machinery
            var spendNorm = spend / 6;                 // 0..1
            var bounding = d.ipBounding;               // 1..5 (IP-term architecture quality)
            var boundNorm = (bounding - 1) / 4;        // 0..1

            // ----- Engineering vs control budget (the explicit trade-off) -----
            // Control spend in this round adds to the cumulative pot drawn from the fixed EUR 12m.
            ds.controlSpend = Math.round((ds.controlSpend + spend) * 10) / 10;
            if (ds.controlSpend > this.BUDGET) ds.controlSpend = this.BUDGET;
            ds.engBudget = Math.round((this.BUDGET - ds.controlSpend) * 10) / 10;
            var engFraction = Math.max(0, ds.engBudget) / this.BUDGET; // 1.0 = all on engineering

            // ----- JOINT CREATIVITY (Bidault's curve) -----
            // Peaks at a trust-leaning sweet spot; falls off toward both full control and full trust.
            var distFromPeak = dial - this.CREATIVITY_PEAK_DIAL;
            var dialCreativity = 100 * Math.exp(-(distFromPeak * distFromPeak) / (2 * this.CREATIVITY_CURVE_WIDTH * this.CREATIVITY_CURVE_WIDTH));
            // Cortexa needs IP to build: too low a tier starves creativity regardless of trust.
            var ipFeed = 0.45 + 0.55 * tierNorm;       // 0.45 (interfaces only) .. 1.0 (open core)
            // Over-lawyering: a gold-plated control regime signals distrust and crowds out creativity.
            var controlDrag = 1 - 0.30 * spendNorm;    // up to -30% at full spend
            // Engineering budget actually funds the work.
            var creativityTarget = dialCreativity * ipFeed * controlDrag * (0.55 + 0.45 * engFraction);

            // ----- TRUST -----
            // Trust rises with a trust-leaning dial and open IP (signals commitment); heavy control
            // machinery signals distrust and erodes it; good bounding builds quiet confidence.
            var trustTarget = 30 + 55 * trustLean + 18 * tierNorm - 28 * spendNorm + 8 * boundNorm;

            // ----- IP RISK -----
            // Rises with how much IP is exposed and how trust-leaning/open the posture is; FALLS hard with
            // good bounding (field-of-use, fore/background split) and modestly with control machinery.
            var ipRiskTarget = 12 + 55 * tierNorm + 22 * trustLean - 42 * boundNorm - 12 * spendNorm;

            // The Round-3 gap: foreground-patent sign-off rule (bounding 5) closes the defection root cause.
            ds.rootCauseFixed = (bounding >= 5) || (period === 4 && d.governance >= 4);

            // ----- Move gauges toward targets (smooth, so each round compounds) -----
            ds.creativity = this._approach(ds.creativity, this._clamp(creativityTarget), 0.62);
            ds.trust = this._approach(ds.trust, this._clamp(trustTarget), 0.6);
            ds.ipRisk = this._approach(ds.ipRisk, this._clamp(ipRiskTarget), 0.6);

            // ----- ROUND 1: diagnosis accuracy nudges the start -----
            // The true dependence is high (~72): Helbion genuinely needs Cortexa for embedded AI.
            var TRUE_DEPENDENCE = 72;
            var depErr = Math.abs(d.dependence - TRUE_DEPENDENCE);
            var diagAccuracy = Math.max(0, Math.round(100 - depErr));
            if (period === 1) {
                // A clear-eyed read that you need the partner nudges trust/creativity; under-reading
                // dependence justifies the control reflex and dampens both.
                var diagNudge = (diagAccuracy - 60) * 0.10;
                ds.trust = this._clamp(ds.trust + diagNudge);
                ds.creativity = this._clamp(ds.creativity + diagNudge);
            }
            ds.diagAccuracy = diagAccuracy;

            // ----- ROUND 3: the defection response -----
            var defectionHandled = null;
            if (period === 3) {
                var resp = d.defection; // 1 litigate .. 5 capitulate; 3-4 = diagnose/repair
                // Truth: intent is low (accident). Clamping down on an accident wrecks trust & creativity.
                var clampness = (3 - Math.min(resp, 3)) / 2; // resp1=>1, resp2=>0.5, resp3+=>0
                var repairness = Math.max(0, (resp - 2)) / 2; // resp3=>0.5, resp4=>1, resp5=>1.5(capped)
                repairness = Math.min(1, repairness);

                if (resp <= 2) {
                    // Escalate / clamp down on an ambiguous, accidental act over a gap you left.
                    ds.trust = this._clamp(ds.trust - 26 * clampness);
                    ds.creativity = this._clamp(ds.creativity - 20 * clampness);
                    ds.ipRisk = this._clamp(ds.ipRisk - 6);   // you do reclaim some control of the IP
                    defectionHandled = 'clampdown';
                } else if (resp === 5) {
                    // Capitulate: peace on the surface, but you signal terms are unenforceable.
                    ds.trust = this._clamp(ds.trust + 4);
                    ds.creativity = this._clamp(ds.creativity + 3);
                    ds.ipRisk = this._clamp(ds.ipRisk + 18); // unilateral action now has no consequence
                    defectionHandled = 'capitulate';
                } else {
                    // Investigate / clarify / recommit — diagnose intent, fix the governance gap.
                    var repairBonusT = 18 * repairness + (this.DEFECTION_INTENT < 40 ? 6 : 0);
                    var repairBonusC = 14 * repairness;
                    ds.trust = this._clamp(ds.trust + repairBonusT);
                    ds.creativity = this._clamp(ds.creativity + repairBonusC);
                    // Repairing only contains IP risk if you ALSO close the term (bounding 5 or recommit fixes it).
                    if (ds.rootCauseFixed) {
                        ds.ipRisk = this._clamp(ds.ipRisk - 16);
                        defectionHandled = 'repaired_rootcause';
                    } else {
                        ds.ipRisk = this._clamp(ds.ipRisk - 4);
                        defectionHandled = 'repaired_symptom';
                    }
                }
            }

            // ----- ROUND 4: recovery governance & board pitch -----
            var govLevel = (period === 4) ? d.governance : null;
            if (period === 4) {
                if (govLevel === 0) {
                    // Revert to build-it-all-ourselves: forfeit the alliance and the embedded-AI window.
                    ds.creativity = this._clamp(ds.creativity * 0.45);
                    ds.trust = this._clamp(ds.trust * 0.4);
                    ds.status = 'dissolved';
                } else {
                    var govNorm = govLevel / 5;
                    ds.trust = this._clamp(ds.trust + 10 * govNorm);
                    ds.creativity = this._clamp(ds.creativity + 12 * govNorm);
                    // Real-options staging + early-warning metrics + blend contain risk durably.
                    ds.ipRisk = this._clamp(ds.ipRisk - 14 * govNorm);
                }
            }

            // ----- Competitive clock: speed as a strategic variable -----
            // Each round burns days. Extreme control + heavy lawyering + tier-1 starvation = slow, over-engineered.
            var slowness = (spendNorm * 0.5 + (1 - trustLean) * 0.35 + (tier === 1 ? 0.25 : 0));
            var daysBurned = period === 1 ? 3 : Math.round(2 + slowness * 4);
            ds.daysLeft = Math.max(0, ds.daysLeft - daysBurned);
            // Sentek risk accumulates when the deal is slow OR when low creativity/trust make Cortexa wander.
            var sentekTick = slowness * 14 + (ds.trust < 45 ? 8 : 0) + (ds.creativity < 35 ? 6 : 0);
            ds.sentekRisk = this._clamp(ds.sentekRisk + sentekTick);

            // ----- ROI: innovation value vs EUR 12m, against the EUR 30m opportunity -----
            // Innovation value (EUR m) scales with creativity AND with how much budget actually funded
            // engineering. Then we net out IP-risk drag (expected loss of crown-jewel value).
            var innovationValue = (ds.creativity / 100) * this.OPPORTUNITY * (0.5 + 0.5 * engFraction);
            var ipLoss = (ds.ipRisk / 100) * 14; // expected EUR m crown-jewel value at risk
            var netValue = innovationValue - ipLoss;
            ds.roi = Math.round((netValue / this.BUDGET) * 100) / 100; // x multiple on the 12m

            // ----- Alliance status (set at R4 unless dissolved above) -----
            if (period === 4 && ds.status !== 'dissolved') {
                if (ds.sentekRisk >= 85) {
                    ds.status = 'lost'; // Sentek signed Cortexa
                    ds.creativity = this._clamp(ds.creativity * 0.5);
                    ds.roi = Math.round((ds.roi * 0.4) * 100) / 100;
                } else if (ds.creativity >= 58 && ds.trust >= 55 && ds.ipRisk <= 45 && ds.roi >= 1.0) {
                    ds.status = 'thriving';
                } else {
                    ds.status = 'transactional'; // low-creativity, contract-policed transaction
                }
            } else if (period < 4) {
                ds.status = 'forming';
            }

            // ----- History -----
            ds.creativityHistory.push(Math.round(ds.creativity));
            ds.trustHistory.push(Math.round(ds.trust));
            ds.ipRiskHistory.push(Math.round(ds.ipRisk));
            ds.roiHistory.push(ds.roi);

            this._updateBars(ds);

            var self = this;
            setTimeout(function() {
                self._updateBriefing(window.mySimulation.state);
            }, 500);

            // v1.1.0 FIX A — expose the composite (clamped 0-100) on the reporting paths.
            var _rs = Math.max(0, Math.min(100, (ds.roi / 2.0) * 100)) * 0.15;
            var _ds = ((this.BUDGET - ds.controlSpend) / this.BUDGET) * 100 * 0.10;
            var _c = Math.max(0, Math.min(100, Math.round(ds.creativity * 0.35 + ds.trust * 0.20 + (100 - ds.ipRisk) * 0.20 + _rs + _ds)));
            ds.score = _c;
            ds.performance = { overallScore: _c };
            return {
                period: period,
                score: _c,
                overallScore: _c,
                trustControl: d.trustControl,
                dependence: d.dependence,
                ipTier: tier,
                controlSpendRound: spend,
                ipBounding: bounding,
                defection: period === 3 ? d.defection : null,
                governance: govLevel,
                diagAccuracy: diagAccuracy,
                creativity: Math.round(ds.creativity),
                trust: Math.round(ds.trust),
                ipRisk: Math.round(ds.ipRisk),
                roi: ds.roi,
                controlSpendTotal: ds.controlSpend,
                engBudget: ds.engBudget,
                daysLeft: ds.daysLeft,
                sentekRisk: Math.round(ds.sentekRisk),
                rootCauseFixed: ds.rootCauseFixed,
                defectionHandled: defectionHandled,
                status: ds.status
            };
        }

        _clamp(v) { return Math.max(0, Math.min(100, v)); }
        _approach(current, target, rate) { return current + (target - current) * rate; }

        _updateBars(ds) {
            var c = document.getElementById('creativityBar');
            var t = document.getElementById('trustBar');
            var r = document.getElementById('ipriskBar');
            var roi = document.getElementById('roiBar');
            if (c) c.style.width = Math.round(ds.creativity) + '%';
            if (t) t.style.width = Math.round(ds.trust) + '%';
            if (r) r.style.width = Math.round(ds.ipRisk) + '%';
            if (roi) roi.style.width = Math.max(0, Math.min(100, Math.round((ds.roi / 2.5) * 100))) + '%';
        }

        _updateBriefing(state) {
            var idx = Math.min((state.currentPeriod || 1) - 1, this.ROUNDS.length - 1);
            var round = this.ROUNDS[idx];

            var lang = 'en';
            try {
                lang = (window.mySimulation && window.mySimulation.language) ? window.mySimulation.language : 'en';
            } catch (e) { lang = 'en'; }

            var briefEl = document.getElementById('briefingText');
            if (briefEl) {
                briefEl.innerHTML = lang === 'es' ? round.briefingEs : round.briefingEn;
            }

            var nameEl = document.getElementById('roundNameDisplay');
            if (nameEl) {
                nameEl.textContent = lang === 'es' ? round.nameEs : round.nameEn;
            }

            var noteEl = document.getElementById('liveLeversNote');
            if (noteEl) {
                var noteKey = 'levers_note_r' + (idx + 1);
                try { noteEl.textContent = window.mySimulation.t(noteKey); } catch (e) {}
            }

            var eventEl = document.getElementById('eventAlert');
            if (eventEl) {
                var eventText = lang === 'es' ? round.eventEs : round.eventEn;
                if (eventText) {
                    eventEl.innerHTML = eventText;
                    eventEl.style.display = 'block';
                } else {
                    eventEl.style.display = 'none';
                }
            }
        }

        setupUI(uiManager) {
            uiManager.bind('currentDay', 'currentPeriod');
            uiManager.bind('maxPeriods', 'maxPeriods');
            uiManager.bind('creativityDisplay', 'domainState.creativity', function(v) { return Math.round(v); });
            uiManager.bind('trustDisplay', 'domainState.trust', function(v) { return Math.round(v); });
            uiManager.bind('ipriskDisplay', 'domainState.ipRisk', function(v) { return Math.round(v); });
            uiManager.bind('roiDisplay', 'domainState.roi', function(v) { return (Math.round(v * 100) / 100).toFixed(2) + 'x'; });
            uiManager.bind('controlSpendDisplay', 'domainState.controlSpend', function(v) {
                return '€' + (Math.round(v * 10) / 10).toFixed(1) + 'm';
            });
            uiManager.bind('engBudgetDisplay', 'domainState.engBudget', function(v) {
                return '€' + (Math.round(v * 10) / 10).toFixed(1) + 'm';
            });
            uiManager.bind('clockDisplay', 'domainState.daysLeft', function(v) { return Math.round(v); });
            uiManager.bind('statusDisplay', 'domainState.status', function(v) {
                var t = window.mySimulation.t;
                if (v === 'thriving') return t('status_thriving');
                if (v === 'transactional') return t('status_transactional');
                if (v === 'lost') return t('status_lost');
                if (v === 'dissolved') return t('status_dissolved');
                return t('status_forming');
            });
        }

        getChartConfig() {
            return {
                gaugeChart: {
                    type: 'line',
                    data: {
                        labels: [],
                        datasets: [
                            { label: 'Joint Creativity', data: [], borderColor: '#14b8a6', backgroundColor: 'rgba(20,184,166,0.12)', borderWidth: 3, fill: false, tension: 0.3 },
                            { label: 'Trust Level', data: [], borderColor: '#3b82f6', backgroundColor: 'rgba(59,130,246,0.12)', borderWidth: 3, fill: false, tension: 0.3 },
                            { label: 'IP Risk', data: [], borderColor: '#f97316', backgroundColor: 'rgba(249,115,22,0.12)', borderWidth: 3, fill: false, tension: 0.3 }
                        ]
                    },
                    options: {
                        responsive: true,
                        maintainAspectRatio: false,
                        plugins: {
                            title: { display: true, text: 'Alliance Gauges by Round' },
                            legend: { position: 'bottom' }
                        },
                        scales: {
                            y: { beginAtZero: true, max: 100, title: { display: true, text: 'Index (0-100)' } }
                        }
                    }
                },
                budgetChart: {
                    type: 'bar',
                    data: {
                        labels: ['Joint Engineering', 'Control Machinery'],
                        datasets: [
                            { label: 'EUR m', data: [], backgroundColor: ['rgba(20,184,166,0.75)', 'rgba(249,115,22,0.75)'], borderColor: ['#14b8a6', '#f97316'], borderWidth: 1 }
                        ]
                    },
                    options: {
                        responsive: true,
                        maintainAspectRatio: false,
                        plugins: {
                            title: { display: true, text: 'EUR 12m Budget Split — Innovation vs. Policing' },
                            legend: { display: false }
                        },
                        scales: {
                            y: { beginAtZero: true, max: 12, title: { display: true, text: 'EUR m' } }
                        }
                    }
                }
            };
        }

        getChartData(state) {
            var ds = state.domainState;
            var labels = ds.creativityHistory.map(function(_, i) { return 'R' + (i + 1); });
            return {
                gaugeChart: {
                    labels: labels,
                    datasets: [
                        { data: ds.creativityHistory },
                        { data: ds.trustHistory },
                        { data: ds.ipRiskHistory }
                    ]
                },
                budgetChart: {
                    labels: ['Joint Engineering', 'Control Machinery'],
                    datasets: [
                        { data: [Math.max(0, ds.engBudget), ds.controlSpend] }
                    ]
                }
            };
        }

        formatCompletionMessage(summary) {
            var t = (window.mySimulation && typeof window.mySimulation.t === 'function')
                ? window.mySimulation.t.bind(window.mySimulation)
                : function (k) { return k; };
            summary = summary || {};
            var score = (summary.totalScore != null) ? summary.totalScore : 0;
            var grade = summary.gradeKey ? t(summary.gradeKey) : '';
            var insights = summary.insights || [];
            var items = insights.map(function (s) { return '<li>' + s + '</li>'; }).join('');
            var metric = function (label, val) {
                return '<div class="al-completion-metric"><span>' + label + '</span><strong>' + val + '</strong></div>';
            };
            var metrics = ''
                + metric(t('comp_creativity_label'), (summary.creativity != null ? summary.creativity : '-'))
                + metric(t('comp_trust_label'), (summary.trust != null ? summary.trust : '-'))
                + metric(t('comp_ip_label'), (summary.ipRisk != null ? summary.ipRisk : '-'))
                + metric(t('comp_roi_label'), (summary.roi != null ? summary.roi : '-') + 'x')
                + metric(t('comp_spend_label'), '\u20ac' + (summary.controlSpend != null ? summary.controlSpend : '-') + 'm');
            return ''
                + '<div class="al-completion">'
                +   '<div class="al-completion-heading">' + t('comp_heading') + '</div>'
                +   '<div class="al-completion-verdict">' + grade + '</div>'
                +   '<div class="al-completion-score">' + t('comp_score_label') + ': <strong>' + score + '</strong> / 100</div>'
                +   '<div class="al-completion-metrics">' + metrics + '</div>'
                +   (items ? '<ul class="al-completion-insights">' + items + '</ul>' : '')
                + '</div>';
        }

        getPerformanceSummary(history) {
            if (!history.length) return {};
            var t = (window.mySimulation && typeof window.mySimulation.t === 'function') ? window.mySimulation.t.bind(window.mySimulation) : function (k) { return k; };
            var last = history[history.length - 1];
            var r = last.results || {};

            var creativity = r.creativity || 0;
            var trust = r.trust || 0;
            var ipRisk = r.ipRisk || 0;
            var roi = r.roi || 0;
            var controlSpend = r.controlSpendTotal || 0;
            var status = r.status || 'transactional';

            // Composite: creativity is the prize (35%), trust (20%), IP risk contained (20%),
            // ROI (15%), budget discipline — share spent on engineering not policing (10%).
            var creativityScore = creativity * 0.35;
            var trustScore = trust * 0.20;
            var ipScore = (100 - ipRisk) * 0.20;
            var roiScore = Math.max(0, Math.min(100, (roi / 2.0) * 100)) * 0.15;
            var disciplineScore = ((this.BUDGET - controlSpend) / this.BUDGET) * 100 * 0.10;
            var totalScore = Math.round(creativityScore + trustScore + ipScore + roiScore + disciplineScore);

            if (status === 'lost' || status === 'dissolved') totalScore = Math.max(0, totalScore - 18);
            if (status === 'thriving') totalScore = Math.min(100, Math.round(totalScore * 1.08));

            var performance = 'Control-Reflex Manager';
            if (totalScore >= 80 && status === 'thriving') performance = 'Alliance Architect';
            else if (totalScore >= 64) performance = 'Capable Co-Development Lead';
            else if (totalScore >= 46) performance = 'Developing Alliance Manager';

            var insights = [];

            // Trust-control curve read-back
            var dials = history.map(function(h) { return (h.results && h.results.trustControl) || 0; });
            var avgDial = Math.round(dials.reduce(function(a, b) { return a + b; }, 0) / dials.length);
            if (avgDial < 40) insights.push(t('ins_dial_control'));
            else if (avgDial > 85) insights.push(t('ins_dial_trust'));
            else insights.push(t('ins_dial_sweet'));

            // Budget discipline
            if (controlSpend >= 4) insights.push(t('ins_controlspend').replace('{amt}', (Math.round(controlSpend * 10) / 10).toFixed(1)));

            // IP architecture / root cause
            var bounded = history.some(function(h) { return h.results && h.results.ipBounding >= 5; });
            if (r.rootCauseFixed) insights.push(t('ins_ip_rootfix'));
            else if (!bounded) insights.push(t('ins_ip_ambiguous'));

            // Defection handling
            var defRound = history.find(function(h) { return h.results && h.results.defectionHandled; });
            if (defRound) {
                var dh = defRound.results.defectionHandled;
                if (dh === 'clampdown') insights.push(t('ins_def_clampdown'));
                else if (dh === 'capitulate') insights.push(t('ins_def_capitulate'));
                else if (dh === 'repaired_rootcause') insights.push(t('ins_def_repaired_root'));
                else if (dh === 'repaired_symptom') insights.push(t('ins_def_repaired_symptom'));
            }

            // Status / outcome
            if (status === 'thriving') insights.push(t('ins_status_thriving'));
            else if (status === 'transactional') insights.push(t('ins_status_transactional'));
            else if (status === 'lost') insights.push(t('ins_status_lost'));
            else if (status === 'dissolved') insights.push(t('ins_status_dissolved'));

            var _gk = (totalScore >= 80 && status === 'thriving') ? 'grade_architect' : totalScore >= 64 ? 'grade_capable' : totalScore >= 46 ? 'grade_developing' : 'grade_reflex';
            if (window.mySimulation && window.mySimulation.state && window.mySimulation.state.domainState) {
                window.mySimulation.state.domainState.score = totalScore;
                window.mySimulation.state.domainState.performance = { overallScore: totalScore, grade: t(_gk) };
            }
            return {
                totalScore: totalScore,
                score: totalScore,
                gradeKey: _gk,
                creativity: creativity,
                trust: trust,
                ipRisk: ipRisk,
                roi: roi,
                controlSpend: controlSpend,
                avgDial: avgDial,
                status: status,
                performance: performance,
                insights: insights
            };
        }

        getHint(state, results) {
            if (!results) return null;
            if (results.status === 'thriving') return window.mySimulation.t('hint_thriving');
            if (results.status === 'lost') return window.mySimulation.t('hint_lost');
            if (results.status === 'dissolved') return window.mySimulation.t('hint_dissolved');
            if (results.defectionHandled === 'clampdown') return window.mySimulation.t('hint_clampdown');
            if (results.defectionHandled === 'capitulate') return window.mySimulation.t('hint_capitulate');
            if (results.controlSpendTotal >= 4) return window.mySimulation.t('hint_overlawyer');
            if (results.trustControl < 35) return window.mySimulation.t('hint_fortress');
            if (results.ipRisk > 60) return window.mySimulation.t('hint_iprisk');
            if (results.sentekRisk > 60) return window.mySimulation.t('hint_clock');
            if (results.creativity < 40) return window.mySimulation.t('hint_lowcreativity');
            return window.mySimulation.t('hint_good_progress');
        }

